			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2444664">
									

<p>I'm not entirely sure how to feel about this one. It's an interesting storytelling gambit burying the common thread through cryptic hints in many incident logs. It was kind of fun puzzling it out (although I did need your hints on the end), but I can't help but feel that there's a large amount of material that is simply unnecessary bureaucrat-ese and chaff. The bits about the psychiatric ward and the burned document, for instance, might make sense as an origin story but didn't really add anything to the overall narrative. They just made it take longer to get to the story.</p>
<p>Also, I don't know if this is intentional, but the details of incident e seem entirely mixed up.<br />
- Hazen, Silvera and Moore are trapped in the wreckage, but the fire dept only recovers Silvera and Moore.<br />
- Hazen and <em>Silvera</em> are ambulanced to the SCP (the others are helicoptered elsewhere), but Hazen and <em>Knotts</em> arrive at the SCP.<br />
Is there a narrative reason for this shuffling that I've missed?</p>

